<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;CATHARINA SIX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Catharina Six is a renowned Dutch art collector born in 1752, known for her exquisite taste in art and her significant role in Amsterdam's cultural scene."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAN BERND BICKER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jan Bernd Bicker is a prominent Dutch politician of the Batavian Republic, born in 1746, who served as a member of the Staatsbewind from 1803 to 1805."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMSTERDAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amsterdam is the city where Catharina Six lived and worked, and where the marriage records and some of the artifacts are located."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BATAVIAN REPUBLIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Batavian Republic is a historical period in Dutch history, during which Jan Bernd Bicker served as a member of the Staatsbewind."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF AMSTERDAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The University of Amsterdam is where Dr. Maria van der Meer works and conducts research on historical figures."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RIJKSMUSEUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rijksmuseum is the museum where Alison Catherine MacGregor and the narrator visit, featuring artworks from the Dutch Golden Age."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rijksmuseum is the museum where letters and portraits of Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker are housed."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. MARIA VAN DER MEER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Maria van der Meer is a leading historian at the University of Amsterdam who confirmed the marriage between Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. PIETER VAN DER VELDEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Pieter van der Velden is a specialist in Dutch art history who provided insights into the cultural and political context of Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker's marriage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALISON CATHERINE MACGREGOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alison Catherine MacGregor is a contemporary researcher who studies Catharina Six's life and legacy, sharing a deep connection with her."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VERMEER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vermeer is mentioned as a painter whose work is featured in the Rijksmuseum, symbolizing the cultural richness of the Dutch Golden Age."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMSTERDAM CITY ARCHIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amsterdam City Archives is the repository of archival documents that confirm the marriage between Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CORRESPONDENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Correspondence includes letters exchanged between Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker, revealing a deep affection and mutual respect."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EYEWITNESS ACCOUNTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eyewitness Accounts include testimonies from contemporaries, corroborating the marriage and providing historical context."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARTWORKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Artworks from the Dutch Golden Age, including a portrait of Catharina Six, are featured in the Rijksmuseum."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STAATSBEWIND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Staatsbewind is the governing body of the Batavian Republic, where Jan Bernd Bicker served as a member."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUTCH GOLDEN AGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dutch Golden Age is the historical period during which Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker lived and worked, characterized by significant cultural and artistic achievements."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMERGING ARTISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emerging Artists are supported by Catharina Six, highlighting her role in promoting and nurturing talent."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ART COLLECTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Art Collector is a role held by Catharina Six, known for her exquisite taste in art and her significant contributions to the cultural scene."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISTORICAL RECORDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Historical Records include archival documents and correspondence that confirm the marriage between Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXHIBITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Exhibits in the Rijksmuseum feature artworks and artifacts related to Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VERMEER'S ARTWORK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vermeer's artwork is mentioned as a piece featured in the Rijksmuseum, symbolizing the cultural richness of the Dutch Golden Age."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTEMPORARIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contemporaries include artists and politicians who knew and interacted with Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker, providing historical context."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALISON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alison is a character whose interest in Catharina's story is described, indicating a personal connection or shared history."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATHARINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Catharina is the subject of Alison's interest, suggesting a significant historical or personal figure."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The narrator is curious about Alison's interest in Catharina's story, indicating a personal connection or shared history."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PORTRAIT OF CATHARINA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ARTIFACT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The portrait of Catharina is described as captivating, suggesting it holds historical or emotional significance."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CURIOSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Curiosity is the driving force behind the narrator's and Alison's interest in Catharina's story."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENIGMATIC SMILE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alison's enigmatic smile adds to the intrigue and mystery surrounding her interest in Catharina's story."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KINDRED SPIRITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The idea of kindred spirits is central to Alison's motivation for studying Catharina's story."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0111</data>
    </node>
